# InfyExchange frontend configuration — single template for dev AND prod.
#
#   dev : leave unset (or copy to `.env`) — vite.config.js proxies /api to the local
#         backend on :8000, so no base URL is needed and CORS is never exercised.
#   prod: set the value in the hosting platform's dashboard (Cloudflare Pages /
#         Vercel) instead of committing a file. Vite inlines it at BUILD time, so a
#         change here always requires a redeploy — it is not read at runtime.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in `.env` / `.env.production` (root .gitignore excludes
# `.env` and `.env.*`; this `.env.example` is the single tracked template).

# Must carry the gateway's /api path and must not end with a slash:
# backend/nginx.conf proxies only /api/ and /health, and src/services/api.js appends
# its own paths (/auth/login, /listings …) to this base. The production build refuses
# a malformed value rather than shipping an SPA that 404s on every request.
#   split deploy (SPA on Pages/Vercel, API on the VM): https://<API_DOMAIN>/api
#   single-origin deploy (nginx serves the SPA too):  /api
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/api
